No superhighway in the world can match the size and scope of America's U.S.

19
00:01:24,942 --> 00:01:25,940
interstate system.

20
00:01:27,080 --> 00:01:33,440
This immense network of highways consists of 55,000 bridges, 100 tunnels,

21
00:01:33,860 --> 00:01:37,960
and a staggering 46,000 miles of concrete and asphalt.

22
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:46,100
Stretched from end to end, it's long enough to circle the earth almost twice.

23
00:01:46,101 --> 00:01:55,100
And in Texas, a state where everything is supersized, America's superhighway is getting even bigger.

24
00:01:56,500 --> 00:02:01,900
In 2003, engineers began a $2.8 billion facelift of Interstate 10,

25
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:06,880
a slice of freeway connecting the bedroom community of Katy to downtown Houston.

26
00:02:09,820 --> 00:02:13,440
500,000 motorists navigate through this corridor each day.

27
00:02:13,441 --> 00:02:19,440
That's roughly 10 times more than when it opened in 1960.

28
00:02:19,441 --> 00:02:24,680
In response, engineers are crafting a 23-mile makeover to quicken the commutes of drivers

29
00:02:24,681 --> 00:02:32,720
heading to and from the fourth largest city in America.

30
00:02:32,721 --> 00:02:39,440
Starting in Katy and heading east to downtown Houston, I-10 bisects two beltways, Highway

31
00:02:39,441 --> 00:02:42,540
8 and I-610.

32
00:02:42,541 --> 00:02:47,400
The corridor's narrowest sections hold 11 lanes of traffic.

33
00:02:47,401 --> 00:02:52,200
I-10's multi-billion dollar makeover will add two toll lanes in each direction, as well

34
00:02:52,201 --> 00:02:58,340
as two additional main lanes and one frontage lane heading west, mirrored by the same additions

35
00:02:58,341 --> 00:03:00,440
heading east.

36
00:03:00,441 --> 00:03:04,960
The final stretch of superhighway will be 20 lanes wide.

37
00:03:04,961 --> 00:03:11,080
It's a $100 million a mile undertaking that runs 24-7.

38
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:16,660
And at mile 17 of the project, paving the new westbound frontage lane is underway.

39
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:23,340
Meet the Slipform Paver, a multitasking mechanical workhorse

40
00:03:23,341 --> 00:03:26,600
that's the quintessential sculptor of the world's superhighways.

41
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:31,400
To pave this road, we have dump trucks which come in.

42
00:03:31,900 --> 00:03:34,520
They'll dump their loads of concrete in front of the paver.

43
00:03:34,960 --> 00:03:37,700
And then the paver will spread that concrete.

44
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:42,360
As the slip form paver reaches the freshly dumped concrete,

45
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:46,640
a set of augured teeth spreads it evenly across the width of the paver's mouth.

46
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:54,360
Vibrators in the paver's steel belly then consolidate the concrete into a homogenous mass.

47
00:03:57,140 --> 00:04:01,700
On the opposite end, the paver's automated tail smooths the concrete lane,

48
00:04:01,701 --> 00:04:03,320
giving it a glossy finish.

49
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:11,960
After the wet concrete is polished, a machine combs grooves into the surface.

50
00:04:11,961 --> 00:04:16,960
The grooves will channel away water when it rains.

51
00:04:16,961 --> 00:04:22,960
Crews also create a rough texture that enables the tires of your car to grip the road.

52
00:04:22,961 --> 00:04:27,960
1,500 feet of new road will be paved tonight.

53
00:04:27,961 --> 00:04:33,960
But this new frontage road will need to cure for seven days before it can open to traffic.

54
